From 6c1641d5dc7a8e61f8bc7effc5c755a84d1e6b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: an ivar that has to be Sized never takes an unsized
 possibility

tsrs 0.18.0 crates/tsrs_fswatch/src/kqueue.rs, `kqueueBackend::compare_dir`
(the user's no-atomic64 patch applied, not involved):

    let mut to_remove = Vec::new();
    to_remove.extend(m.keys().filter_map(|p| {
        let rest = p.strip_prefix(&dir_start)?; .. Some(p.clone())
    }));
    for p in to_remove {
        sub.dir_watch.events.remove(&p);            // fn remove(&self, path: &str)
        .. .filter(|(d, _)| *d == &p || is_descendant(d, &p)) ..
    }

    <null> error:0: Unsized type not valid here - str

`to_remove`'s element type comes only from `extend`. Its lookup pauses
(f4932480): `Extend<T> for Vec<T>` and `Extend<&T> for Vec<T> where T: Copy`
both match `Vec<_>` fuzzily, and the `filter_map` closure stays uncoerced while
the call is open. Meanwhile `*d == &p` reduced to `String: PartialEq<_>` (impl
list ByteString, ByteStr, str, &str, Cow<str>, String) and `remove(&p)` gave
a `&_ -> &str` destination. The plain "IVar possibilities" stage, which runs
before the deferred-methods stage, took `str` through "Bounded and possible
type". The ivar is flagged Sized (Vec's `T`), so equating it errored, from
check_ivar_poss's static null span.

check_ivar_poss computed `allow_unsized`, but only the late filter of
`possible_tys` read it. "Source/Destination type", "Bounded and possible
type", "One possibility (before ivar removal)", "Most accepting pointer
class", the least/most-restrictive rules and the Assume "Suitable option"
picked a type without that test (the others go through
check_ivar_poss__fails_bounds, which has it). These rules now skip a type that
is unsized when the ivar has to be Sized. Such a pick always ended in this
error (set_ivar_to -> require_sized makes the same test), so code that
compiled before is unaffected. Here the stage leaves the ivar alone, the
deferred-methods stage commits `extend`, and the element type is `String` as
in rustc. A genuinely unsized use is still rejected, now from the node's span.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp
index d03f174f..82ec6062 100644
